title: 1928 RSDRP Party Congress
subtitle: The 1928 Party Congress has finally arrived. We will choose our Party Programme for the coming election, and for the next two-years.
tags: event
view-if: year = 1928 and month == 2
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/programme.jpg
on-arrival: ideology = "centrist"
new-page: true

= 1928 Party Congress of the Russian Social Democratic Labor Party

the Bi-Annual Party Congress has finally arrived! For the past few days, our members have bickered, debated, and voted on the party programme that will serve us for the next two years.

- @left: With the support of the Labor Left and sympathetic Centrists, the Internationalists have managed to sway the Programme towards Class Struggle and Proletarian Internationalism.
- @centrist: Supported by most of the Left and Right, the Menshevik Center passes their Programme, hopefully their moderation of the Party Left and Right can resolve our internal divisions.
- @labor: The Labor-wing, managing to sway sympathetic leftists and rightists, pass their economic-focused Programme of focusing on Soviet-Government cooperation, Labor Reform, and results.
- @reform: Rallying the Laborites and sympathetic Centrists, the Liquidationists have shockingly come out on top, removing most mentions of revolution from the Programme and replacing them with democratic, reformist, and ethical socialist language.

@left
choose-if: left_strength + center_strength >= reformist_strength
unavailable-subtitle: The Party Left is unable to convince Left-Laborites and Centrist to support their Internationalist programme.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "left") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "left"; left_strength += 10; communist_coalition += 1; left_dissent -= 5; z_relation -= 3; dvp_relation -= 5; nationalization_support += 1; kpd_relation += 3

With the support of the Labor Left and sympathetic Centrists, the Internationalists have managed to sway the Programme towards Class Struggle and Proletarian Internationalism.

@centrist
choose-if: labor_strength + center_strength + left_strength + reformist_strength >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: The Party Center lacks the votes to... wait, what? This shouldn't even be an option, how do the hell did you acheive this?
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "centrist") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "centrist"; center_strength += 10; center_dissent -= 10; left_dissent -= 5; reformist_dissent -= 5

Supported by most of the Party, the Menshevik Center passes their Orthodox Programme. Hopefully their moderation of the Party Left and Right can resolve our internal divisions.

@labor
choose-if: labor_strength >= left_strength
unavailable-subtitle: The Labor-wing lacks the votes to push it's own agenda, it's left- and right-leaning members have opted to support the agendas of other factions.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "labor") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "labor"; labor_strength += 10; wtb_support += 1; labor_dissent -= 5; kpd_relation -= 3

The Labor-wing, managing to sway sympathetic Centrists and Rightists, pass their economic-focused Programme of focusing on Soviet-Government cooperation, Labor Reform, and pragmatism.

@reform
choose-if: reformist_strength + labor_strength >= left_strength + center_strength
unavailable-subtitle: The Party Right lacks the strength and charisma to push it's evolutionary programme.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "reformist") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "reformist"; reformist_strength += 10; democratization += 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; z_relation += 5; dvp_relation += 5; kpd_relation -= 8; moderate_plan_support += 1

Rallying the Laborites and sympathetic Centrists, the Liquidationists have shockingly come out on top, removing most mentions of revolution from the Programme and replacing them with democratic, reformist, and ethical socialist language.

@changed
on-arrival: left_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; reformist_dissent -= 5

We have concluded the Congress. Many in the party are excited for the future, but some are saddened by the party programme.